{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFYgXvQov5XEVD3rf4SN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Without an install, both subcommands exit non-zero\n\nI added `hermes-tiiny-router ctl ...` and `hermes-tiiny-router route-check ...`, and all four checklist items are done. The full `npm test` passes: 12 Node tests and the Python suite.\n\n**What the commands do:** both run a script from the installed plugin, `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/scripts/`, not the copy in the package. `ctl` runs `tiiny_ctl.py` and `route-check` runs `route_check.py`, each with the system `python3 -B`. Every argument after the subcommand goes to the script unchanged, including `--help`. The command exits with the script's exit code. If the script isn't installed, it prints a message saying to run `install` first and exits 1. If the script is killed by a signal, the command exits 1. The code is in `src/passthrough.ts`, and `src/cli.ts` sends the two subcommands to it.\n\n**How it's tested** (`test/passthrough.test.ts`): the real scripts need a Tiiny device, so each test installs into a temporary Hermes home and then replaces the installed script with a small Python stand-in. The stand-in records the arguments it receives and exits with a code the test picks. The tests check:\n1. Awkward arguments (an empty string, `two words`, `--help`, `-h`, `$HOME`, `*`) arrive unchanged for both commands.\n2. Exit codes 0, 3 and 42 come back unchanged for both commands.\n3. Both commands exit non-zero when nothing is installed.\n\n**One departure from strict TDD:** I wrote both subcommands in the first step, so the tests for items 2–4 passed the first time they ran. To make sure they actually test something, I briefly broke the code for each one: sent `route-check` to the wrong script, turned exit codes into just 0 or 1, and made the not-installed case return 0. Each test failed as it should, and I put the code back.\n\nI also added a short note to `AGENTS.md` on how these commands find their scripts and how to test them with a stand-in. Everything is committed except `.redeye/notes.md`, as instructed. There were no `__pycache__` folders to clean up."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":317,"cache_read_input_tokens":60479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":317},"output_tokens":712,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88d75eb6-f540-4294-8089-c65a5d5b0901","uuid":"bb2ff831-91c1-4f6c-b64b-4c42b47c18b7","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:48:13.823Z","request_id":"req_011ChFYgXm1411NWWqZ5swo5"}
